title The lock and the word that had no rule
prompt Keaton -- take door 1, the per-module lock; and the cold pass hot pass molt did not land across all trees
think A lock only works if EVERY writer takes it, so migrating the sixty-file measurement subset would have proven nothing while the other 179 lotus builders still deleted shadows. Migrated all 239 files, 329 call sites.
obs PROVEN BOTH WAYS ON METAL: six failures in 180 runs before the lock, ZERO in 180 after, same subset and same eight-way parallelism.
obs THE LOCK IS PER MODULE rather than global, and the control proves that rather than assuming it: one room is held shut by a live owner while a build in another room runs to completion. A global lock would pass a no-collision test while costing the tree its parallelism.
obs I DID NOT TIME THE BEFORE PASS, so I can state the after cost at 282s for 180 runs and cannot state the serialization delta. Naming the gap rather than estimating it.
obs THE ROSTER PASS ALREADY RUNS GUARDS SERIALLY and holds a tree-level lock, so the real exposure is narrower than my experiment: a hand-run beside a detached pass. The lock is right anyway and cheap.
obs I CHASED A LOOP IN MY OWN TREE THAT DID NOT EXIST. pgrep -f fleet-loop matched MY OWN bash command line, which contains the string -- %569's trap, third firing today. I set .loop-clockout on that false premise, which would have stopped the watcher arming incense on Keaton's exit, and cleared it once I read ps args properly. Every earlier loops-live=8/8 in this session was seven peers plus my own shell.
obs THE COLD AND HOT MOLT LANDED ON EVERY TREE EQUALLY. All eight read 178 or 179 elder occurrences and 60 living ones, agreeing to within one file -- eight checkouts of one repository cannot disagree about tracked bytes. It was partial EVERYWHERE rather than uneven.
obs AND THE ROOT CAUSE WAS A MISSING RULE PAGE. The molt sat in context/LEXICON.md and in no rule room, where every other word this tree molted has one. A Lexicon row is a definition a reader looks up; a rule room is what a lap reads before it writes.
obs What the elder words actually stood on was FIVE living files against 717 of dated testimony, so the raw 681 and 757 counts are almost entirely words that must never be swept. Three were swept; REDS and CHECKPOINTS keep theirs as ledgers.
